(7029509, 1066328, 86218, '<td valign="top">A truly beautiful image. Subtle lines and wonderful autumn Colours. Love the grass in the f/g. Top three for me</td>', 'A truly beautiful image. Subtle lines and wonderful autumn Colours. Love the grass in the f/g. Top three for me', '2013-04-30 07:19:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7029577, 1066608, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>To me this speaks of boating on the river has ended for the season. Fall leaves lay scattered on the shore (ground) while the boats lay ''beached'' til the season turns warm once again. The weathered window reflects back the rust/brown hues of Autumn.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  To me this speaks of boating on the river has ended for the season. Fall leaves lay scattered on the shore (ground) while the boats lay ''beached'' til the season turns warm once again. The weathered window reflects back the rust/brown hues of Autumn.', '2013-04-30 10:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7029582, 1065749, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>You have some beautiful tones of oranges, golds, and greens in the leaves. That is the composition''s strength and the I feel the area you should play up. As it stands now the main focus gets lost with too much empty space of the trees on the opposite bank and the less than flattering color of the river. My suggestion is to zoom in closer to those Autumn leaves and if you want to still show a portion of the river perhaps (provided you had the time to do so) a different time or day when it would reflect more of the sky or be less cloudy brown.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. You have some beautiful tones of oranges, golds, and greens in the leaves. That is the composition''s strength and the I feel the area you should play up. As it stands now the main focus gets lost with too much empty space of the trees on the opposite bank and the less than flattering color of the river. My suggestion is to zoom in closer to those Autumn leaves and if you want to still show a portion of the river perhaps (provided you had the time to do so) a different time or day when it would reflect more of the sky or be less cloudy brown.', '2013-04-30 10:22:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7029584, 1065943, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I like that zoom effect especially when paired with the yellows and oranges. It implies that the colors of autumn are ''zooming'' in on the leaves in the center - soon the colors will change and Fall will be here. You have a good foundation but I think it still needs a bit of work to make the composition resonate even stronger. First off, the colors are a bit dark had they been more bold and vibrant yellows and oranges it would project the idea even stronger. Perhaps time of day to get better colors or enhance in PP would get those hues. Second, the branch with leaves in the center could be sharper in focus &amp; detail. I''m guessing that this was taken without a tripod to keep the focal point rocky steady. Recommendation is to steady the camera on something that will not move during the shot or have a tripod handy.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I like that zoom effect especially when paired with the yellows and oranges. It implies that the colors of autumn are ''zooming'' in on the leaves in the center - soon the colors will change and Fall will be here. You have a good foundation but I think it still needs a bit of work to make the composition resonate even stronger. First off, the colors are a bit dark had they been more bold and vibrant yellows and oranges it would project the idea even stronger. Perhaps time of day to get better colors or enhance in PP would get those hues. Second, the branch with leaves in the center could be sharper in focus & detail. I''m guessing that this was taken without a tripod to keep the focal point rocky steady. Recommendation is to steady the camera on something that will not move during the shot or have a tripod handy.', '2013-04-30 10:28:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7029586, 1066663, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great light and details captured in this shot. I like the idea you are presenting to me and the audience. However, the Autumn leaf takes a back seat to all those bold and vibrant blue flowers and deep green of the grass. Those flowers speak Spring to me - not Summer where it will naturally fall into Autumn. I think had you cropped closer and trimmed much of the field of flowers out of the frame to put the focus solely on the leaf it would project Autumn more strongly. I suspect that the leaf was planted there and as such you would have control over the arrangement of elements. If so, then a leaf that is less crumpled to show off the full shape would have been best. It would show off more details in the leaf and be more readily identifiable as a leaf.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great light and details captured in this shot. I like the idea you are presenting to me and the audience. However, the Autumn leaf takes a back seat to all those bold and vibrant blue flowers and deep green of the grass. Those flowers speak Spring to me - not Summer where it will naturally fall into Autumn. I think had you cropped closer and trimmed much of the field of flowers out of the frame to put the focus solely on the leaf it would project Autumn more strongly. I suspect that the leaf was planted there and as such you would have control over the arrangement of elements. If so, then a leaf that is less crumpled to show off the full shape would have been best. It would show off more details in the leaf and be more readily identifiable as a leaf.', '2013-04-30 10:36:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7029606, 1066387, 118154, '<td valign="top">Good image,stands out well.</td>', 'Good image,stands out well.', '2013-04-30 11:05:14.000000', NULL, 1),
